{
	title: 'Restart scopes: local, host, both, all',
	spec: 'The shared command list has one /restart command with scopes. Bare /restart and /restart local restart only this client: the terminal exits with the restart code, the web page reloads. Ctrl-R is /restart local everywhere: the terminal emergency path, and the browser native reload on the web; /keys shows it as /restart local (command-list keyArgs), and completion offers local, host, both and all. /restart host, both and all run on the host (src/host/commands/restart.ts), which replies and then exits with the restart code after a short flush delay; peers take over as usual, whichever wins, whatever code it runs. both: the client that typed it marks itself and restarts (terminal) as soon as its link changes after the mark, or reloads (web) once the host is gone and back. all: the host first sends every connected client a restart event, which marks it the same way. Delivery to connected clients is best effort: a client asleep or disconnected then is not tracked. When the client is the host process, local and host restart the same process once. Existing command ids, takeover and turn recovery are reused; restart adds no new lifecycle state or permission tier.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Host code may not import client code (conventions.test.ts layers): the host command exits through restartProcess.run, which main.ts points at terminal.restart so raw mode is left first. Web restart state lives in src/web/restart.ts, and the web draft store in src/web/draft-store.ts, keeping web/app.ts under the 400-line limit.'
	],
